# Peter Kamau - IYF S10 Week 01

Welcome to my IYF Season 10 Week 01 repository! This contains all the tasks and projects completed during the first week of the program.

## About Me

Hi! My name is Peter Kamau. I am passionate about technology and building digital technology solutions.

## Tasks & Projects Structure

### 📁 Lesson 1 Tasks

#### 1.1 Personal Portfolio Page
- **File**: `Lesson 1 Tasks/index.html`
- **Format**: HTML
- **Description**: Basic personal portfolio page with introduction, hobbies, and contact information

#### 1.2 DevTools Exploration
- **File**: `Lesson 1 Tasks/devtools-exploration.md`
- **Format**: Markdown
- **Description**: Analysis of three different websites using browser developer tools
  - example.com (HTML tags analysis)
  - developer.mozilla.org (Navigation and search structure)
  - nse.co.ke (Form elements and HTML structure)

### 📁 Lesson 2 Tasks

#### 2.1 Semantic HTML Conversion
- **File**: `Lesson 2 Tasks/Semetric-Conversion.html`
- **Format**: HTML
- **Description**: Conversion of HTML content to semantic HTML5 elements

#### 2.2 Contact Form
- **File**: `Lesson 2 Tasks/Contact-Form.html`
- **Format**: HTML
- **Description**: Functional contact form with validation and user feedback

#### 2.3 Accessibility Report
- **File**: `Lesson 2 Tasks/Accessibility-report.md`
- **Format**: Markdown
- **Description**: Accessibility analysis and improvements for web content

#### 2.4 Multi-Page Portfolio Structure
- **Files**: 
  - `Lesson 2 Tasks/multi-pages Portfolio structure/index.html` (Homepage)
  - `Lesson 2 Tasks/multi-pages Portfolio structure/about.html` (About page)
  - `Lesson 2 Tasks/multi-pages Portfolio structure/portfolio.html` (Projects page)
  - `Lesson 2 Tasks/multi-pages Portfolio structure/contact.html` (Contact page)
  - `Lesson 2 Tasks/multi-pages Portfolio structure/css/style.css` (Stylesheet)
- **Format**: HTML + CSS
- **Description**: Complete multi-page portfolio website with consistent navigation and professional styling

## Technical Skills Demonstrated

- **HTML5**: Semantic markup, forms, accessibility
- **CSS3**: Responsive design, styling, layout
- **JavaScript**: Basic interactivity and form handling
- **Git & GitHub**: Version control and repository management
- **Web Accessibility**: ARIA labels, semantic structure
- **Responsive Design**: Mobile-first approach

